"Albarkatun Ƙasa na Nijeriya\",\n    \"type\": \"diagram\",\n    \"depictEn\": \"A balanced Nigeria resource landscape divided into connected scenes: Northern farmland and livestock, a river used for water and fishing, a managed forest with wildlife habitat, a neutral mineral-rock inset, and distant regulated oil and gas facilities; arrows connect resources to food, work, and manufactured goods.\",\n    \"labelsHa\": [\"Ƙasa\", \"Ruwa\", \"Dazuzzuka\", \"Ma’adanai\", \"Man fetur\", \"Iskar gas\"],\n    \"safetyNote\": \"No company logos, political figures, ethnic ownership claims, unsafe mining, spills, flames, child labour, or suggestion that oil and gas are Nigeria's only resources; show girls and boys observing from a safe public viewpoint.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"p5-socs-02\",\n    \"imagePath\": \"images/p5-socs-02.png\",\n    \"titleEn\": \"Conservation of Natural Resources\",\n    \"titleHa\": \"Kula da Albarkatun Ƙasa\",\n    \"type\": \"comparison\",\n    \"depictEn\": \"A two-column Northern Nigerian community comparison: on the left, responsibly managed grazing, tree planting, a closed water tap, reuse of containers, and small solar and wind installations; on the right, non-graphic overgrazed ground, an open dripping tap, and tree stumps, with clear green action arrows toward restoration.\",\n    \"labelsHa\": [\"Dasa itatuwa\", \"Rufe famfo\", \"Kiyaye ciyayi\", \"Makamashin rana\", \"Makamashin iska\"],\n    \"safetyNote\": \"Keep degradation mild and educational; no distressed people or animals, no dangerous tools in children's hands, no claim that one livelihood group causes all damage, and no brand or commercial-energy promotion.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"p5-socs-03\",\n    \"imagePath\": \"images/p5-socs-03.png\",\n    \"titleEn\": \"Environmental Pollution\",\n    \"titleHa\": \"Gurɓata Muhalli\",\n    \"type\": \"comparison\",\n    \"depictEn\": \"Three paired panels labeled air, water, and land: each contrasts a mildly polluted scene with a clean community response—reduced smoke and planted trees, protected water with waste kept out, and sorted rubbish placed in bins while drains remain clear.\",\n    \"labelsHa\": [\"Iska\", \"Ruwa\", \"Ƙasa\", \"Kwandon shara\", \"Kiyaye magudana\", \"Dasa itatuwa\"],\n    \"safetyNote\": \"No graphic illness, dead wildlife, hazardous chemical symbols, identifiable factories, children touching sharp waste, or climate-disaster imagery; adults handle any unsafe waste and children only observe or use ordinary bins.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"p5-socs-04\",\n    \"imagePath\": \"images/p5-socs-04.png\",\n    \"titleEn\": \"Disaster Preparedness and Safety\",\n    \"titleHa\": \"Shiri da Kariya Lokacin Bala’i\",\n    \"type\": \"diagram\",\n    \"depictEn\": \"A calm school safety-plan diagram showing a marked exit route, a safe assembly point, a teacher leading pupils away from simplified flood, fire, and road-accident warning icons, plus radio and town-crier alert symbols; trained adult responders appear only as distant neutral icons.\",\n    \"labelsHa\": [\"Hanyar fita\", \"Wurin taruwa\", \"Wuri mai aminci\", \"Gargadi\", \"Masu horo\"],\n    \"safetyNote\": \"No injury, panic, bodies, active rescue instruction, dangerous proximity to water, fire, vehicles, fuel, or glass; no emergency-service logo or unsupported phone number; children follow adults and never perform rescue.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"p5-socs-05\",\n    \"imagePath\": \"images/p5-socs-05.png\",\n    \"titleEn\": \"The Nigerian Constitution and Rule of Law\",\n    \"titleHa\": \"Kundin Tsarin Mulkin Nijeriya da Bin Doka\",\n    \"type\": \"diagram\",\n    \"depictEn\": \"A neutral civic balance diagram with an unbranded book titled in Hausa at the centre, equal paths leading to government, citizens, and a simple courthouse, and small symbols for rights, duties, elections, evidence, and public property; all people stand at the same level before the law.\",\n    \"labelsHa\": [\"Kundin tsarin mulki\",